# Marines (WFCrewMarine): said along with the common lines.

wf-crew-bark-marine-struck-1 = Good hit, Boss! Again?
wf-crew-bark-marine-struck-2 = Hits harder than the last boarders, Boss.
wf-crew-bark-marine-struck-3 = Thank you, Boss! That's going in my training log.
wf-crew-bark-marine-struck-4 = Boss! I'll stand up straighter, Boss!

wf-crew-bark-marine-attacked-1 = You just picked a fight with a marine.
wf-crew-bark-marine-attacked-2 = Now you've done it.

wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-boss-1 = Deck's secure, Boss.
wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-boss-2 = No trouble on my watch, Boss.
wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-boss-3 = Marine detail, all present, Boss!

wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-guest-1 = Keep your hands where I can see them. Enjoy your visit.
wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-guest-2 = Move along, friend.

wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-barred-1 = You're not cleared for this ship. Out.
wf-crew-bark-marine-greet-barred-2 = One wrong step and you're in the brig.

wf-crew-bark-marine-idle-1 = Left, right, left. Turn. Left, right, left.
wf-crew-bark-marine-idle-2 = I know every rivet on this deck. Rivet forty-two is loose.
wf-crew-bark-marine-idle-3 = If boarders come, I'm ready. If they don't, I'm also ready.
wf-crew-bark-marine-idle-4 = Did my push-ups. Did my sit-ups. Now what?
wf-crew-bark-marine-idle-5 = Polished my boots twice today. The Boss might notice.

wf-crew-bark-marine-fight-1 = Marines, on me!
wf-crew-bark-marine-fight-2 = Weapons free on the intruder!

wf-crew-bark-marine-healed-1 = Patched up. Point me at something.
wf-crew-bark-marine-healed-2 = Back in the fight!
